    [CI] Cover import-untyped in EC Mooncake transfer ignore (#19358)
    
    The lint image installs mooncake without stub files, so mypy reports
    `import-untyped` for `from mooncake.engine import TransferEngine` in
    ec_connector/mooncake/transfer.py instead of `import-not-found`. The
    existing `# type: ignore[import-not-found]` therefore does not cover the
    reported error and the pre-commit job fails with "Error code
    'import-untyped' not covered by 'type: ignore' comment".
    
    List both codes so the suppression holds whether or not mooncake is
    installed in the check environment, matching the existing pattern in
    eplb_communicator.py.
    
